      "content": "It is completely understandable that platitudes feel hollow when you are in such deep, persistent pain. That feeling of being stuck between states is a profound kind of suffering, and it is valid. Since the typical script doesn't fit your reality, perhaps reaching out to a therapist who specializes in grief or existential distress could offer a different kind of understanding. They can meet you where you are without trying to force a timeline for \"better.\"",
      "source": "target",
